<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40656" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-crūdesco</span></b> ,
			dŭi, 3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i>, <i>to
				become raw again.</i> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, of wounds, <i>to break
				open afresh</i>: nunc autem hoc tam gravi vulnere etiam illa,
			quae consanuisse videbantur, recrudescunt, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 4,
				6, 2</span></i>. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">recrudescente Manlianā seditione,</span>”
				<i>breaking out again</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 6,
					18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">recruduit pugna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 19 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">recruduit soporatus odor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Curt.
					7, 1, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">recrudescit nefas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Phoen. 231</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
